class:: TLevyRand
summary:: Triggered one-sided Lévy-distribution sampler
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/TStableRand, Classes/TCauchyRand

description::

Computes code::location + scale/(Z*Z):: for a standard normal code::Z::. Values too near zero are retried at most 64 times before returning the largest finite float.

The distribution has one-sided support beginning at location and a very heavy tail. Extreme finite values are expected and may require explicit user-side limiting before direct audio use.

Like link::Classes/TStableRand::, it represents a stable-family heavy tail; unlike the general sampler, its support and alpha-one-half construction are fixed and explicit.

subsection:: Distribution shape

image::levy-density.png#One-sided Lévy densities with location = 0 and scale = 0.5, 1, and 2, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum over a finite display interval. The density begins above the location and retains a very long right tail.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: location
Lower support location.
argument:: scale
Nonnegative Lévy scale. Invalid scale returns location.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial value.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TLevyRand.kr(0, 1, Impulse.kr(4)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(TLevyRand.kr(100, 80, Impulse.kr(6)).clip(80, 4000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

